{
 "artifact_type": "omp_ninfer_measurement",
 "schema_version": 1,
 "experiment": "EXP-055",
 "title": "Row-blocked small-T projections and a conflict-free Q4 gate/up MMA shorten the MTP3 decode round",
 "generated_utc": "2026-09-25T16:10:00Z",
 "status": "passed",
 "question": "Can the verify-pass kernels EXP-054 ranked recover a material share of the MTP3 decode round without changing any output bit, and does the change hold on both shipped lanes?",
 "answer": "Yes on the RTX 5090: row-blocking the small-T Q4/Q5 SIMT projections and padding and double-buffering the Q4 gate/up MMA staging cut a 26K-context verify round from 17.75 to 16.08 ms in an A/B/B/A of the packaged release build (+10.3% to +11.0% decode tok/s from a seed context to 31K), with output bytes identical at all 32 kernel/extent points, the 89-case role corpus identical and 130,048-token retrieval exact. On the RTX 4090 the Q5 split2 row pair was slower (MLP down +19% at T=4), so the first candidate decoded 2.7% slower in the lane's C1 benchmark; keeping one row per warp for split2 on the native lanes turned that into +2.8% (157.89 vs 153.54 tok/s).",
 "decision": "Ship RTX 5090 runtime v0.6.10-qwen38-5090-beta.1 from 8cc0810a and RTX 4090 runtime v0.6.8-qwen38-4090-beta.1 from 5a774841 (alphastorm/ninfer#44), each qualified on its packaged bytes; publication is the founder's. At 90% of the floor 1.40 ms (8.7%) of the round remains recoverable, led by MLP down, GDN query/key and attention decode.",
 "method": {
  "candidate_window": "2026-09-25 13:50-14:11Z on the owner RTX 5090 with production held and stopped: a private-launcher sweep of the final vs 86733c0e kernels (cold L2, output byte comparison), 8 oracle tests, public op benches, ninfer_bench A/B/B/A, a 26K nsys graph-node trace, then a candidate server on production arguments for the role corpus and profile gates",
  "release_window": "2026-09-25 14:35-15:31Z, stock OMP proof rerun 15:32-15:36Z: the packaged 8cc0810a binaries layered on the runtime-image base as arm pkg-8cc0810a with production's serving arguments: oracle tests, public op benches, A/B/B/A, role corpus, then window 7's lane evidence set",
  "bench": "ninfer_bench --kv-dtype bf16 --prefill-chunk 1024 --mtp-draft-tokens 3 --lm-head-draft -n 256 -pg '1024,256;26000,256;31000,256' -r 3 --warmup 1; A/B/B/A = baseline, change, change, baseline",
  "rtx4090": "the owner RTX 4090 host, MSVC/vcpkg sm_89 builds in the lane's tree: oracle tests and public op benches; tools/qualification/qualify_native.py's 15 phases, which build, package and install the candidate and include 130,048-token retrieval, restart, rollback, security, the stock OMP client and the C1 benchmark"
 },
